Add this to the existing vercel.json in ghl-mcp-remote (merge into the "crons" array
if one already exists):

{
  "crons": [
    {
      "path": "/api/cron/monthly-content-report",
      "schedule": "0 8 1 * *"
    }
  ]
}

This runs at 8:00 AM UTC on the 1st of each month and pulls data for the prior month.

---

Env vars to add in Vercel project settings:

GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID       from Cloud Console: Credentials -> OAuth client ID
                             (Desktop app type)
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET   from the same OAuth client
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN   generated via scripts/get-refresh-token.js while
                             logged in as info@utahreia.org (already done)
GA4_PROPERTY_ID              the GA4 property ID tied to GTM-PQBDRK4V
OPUSCLIP_API_KEY             OpusClip API key
OPUSCLIP_ORG_ID              org_1jmm83im4i24q8DyKJQXG
GHL_API_KEY                  already set in this repo (Private Integration
                             token); reused as-is, no new var needed
SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID        1RwVLFMhkfjWFXFpMaSlq86Hj0T8YOJv6YKQi53LTPic
                             (already created; owned by info@utahreia.org)
CRON_SECRET                  any random string; also set in the cron config as
                             the bearer token Vercel sends

Note: Ahrefs is commented out in the cron endpoint. Their API requires an
Enterprise plan; revisit once that's confirmed, then uncomment the import,
the Promise.all entry, and the tab write in api/cron/monthly-content-report.ts,
plus set AHREFS_API_KEY.

npm packages to add: googleapis, @google-analytics/data, open (dev dependency,
only needed to run get-refresh-token.js locally, not in the deployed function)
